## Graphics & Design

| Windows | Linux Alternative | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Paint | [Pinta](https://www.pinta-project.com) | Simple image editor |
| Photoshop | [GIMP](https://www.gimp.org) | Powerful free image editor |
| Illustrator | [Inkscape](https://inkscape.org) | Free vector graphics editor |
| Lightroom | [Darktable](https://www.darktable.org) | Free photo processing |

::: info What about Photoshop?
Photoshop itself doesn't have a Linux version. GIMP covers most use cases, but if you need Photoshop specifically, it can sometimes run through **Wine** or a Windows VM. Check [WineHQ](https://appdb.winehq.org) for compatibility.
:::

## Gaming

| Windows | Linux Alternative | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Steam (Windows games) | [Steam + Proton](https://store.steampowered.com) | Runs most Windows games natively |
| Epic Games | [Heroic Launcher](https://heroicgameslauncher.com) | Epic & GOG games on Linux |
| GOG Galaxy | [Heroic Launcher](https://heroicgameslauncher.com) | GOG games support included |
| Xbox App | — | Not available, use Steam/Heroic |

::: tip Check compatibility first
Before switching, check [ProtonDB](https://www.protondb.com) to see how well your games run on Linux. Most popular titles work great, especially on Fedora with up-to-date drivers.
:::

